# Innvntory — Git attributes
#
# Purpose: keep the repository consistent across contributor machines, and
# guarantee that the supplied source-of-truth and reference material is stored
# byte-for-byte exactly as it was supplied.
#
# Rule order matters: later patterns override earlier ones.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default text handling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auto-detect text vs binary. Store text with LF in the repository; check out
# with the platform's native line ending. This is what core.autocrlf=true
# already does on its own — it is stated here so behaviour does not depend on
# each contributor's local Git configuration.
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplied source-of-truth and reference material — DO NOT CONVERT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md §5: these files must not be modified, renamed, moved, converted,
# overwritten, or deleted. `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion so the
# committed blob is byte-identical to the file as supplied, byte-for-byte.
#
# Note: gitattributes patterns are split on whitespace, so a literal space in a
# pattern is not reliable. The directory name uses `?` as a single-character
# wildcard for the space. Verified with:
#   git check-attr text -- "Design Refrence/404.html"
Innvntory.md.txt -text
DESIGN-cursor.md -text
Design?Refrence/** -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary assets — never line-ending converted
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.webp -text
*.ico -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated and vendored output — not stored in this repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed for completeness so that if these ever appear they are treated as
# binary artefacts rather than diffable source.
node_modules/** -text -diff
dist/** -text -diff
build/** -text -diff
coverage/** -text -diff